{"kind":"report","text":"N1 current-model handoff under 6dc, based on accepted ac54a18b6d011a5efeaa9a9a3e4980c3d353c6d3. Later f6d80 advances only survey prose; both package trees are exactly 30727ff4aa5502c45f391df36b40546f2855016b. Reused FULL historical e585 findings and original 53016 scope, not another review of the old 999-line Room design. Root FULL read current task, original request, e585 report, ec3c editor specification and owner decisions 531422/0cb78, both bounded peer seals and meaningful current native spans. No runtime route, API, Source approval or whole N1 closure follows.\n\nDecision/dependency map:\n1. Retained proposal identity: current Page manifestContent verifies complete authenticated entry, full scope incarnation, item/opening hash, signature/target/author relationship and exact path/digest/UTF8 size/content. New editor task DTO must retain service/directory/full membership and key, rules/destination, full source lane incarnation, selected manifest ID and opening FactRef/hash, actual signed source base/path/digest/size. Current ChangeView returns scope ID and content, omitting some full proof identity; this is a handoff gap, not a demonstrated forged-base defect. Owner: existing N1 A1/A3 plus Page/editor bc78. Keep original source separate from newly sampled published base and NEW lane/version; no silent rebinding.\n2. Base-file authority: a signed proposal's base string, arbitrary ancestor/object ID, public rendered Site or configured host is not permission to disclose literal editable bytes. Name a permitted immutable base using exact repository/directory/destination incarnation, recorded publication/first-head fact and actual written receipt/fetched proof. Adopt the literal-content reader policy and revalidate current membership/delegation/revocation before content, cache hits and each new page. Root current Reads/signed-read spans establish existing scoped/causal checks, not generic whole-Git authority. Owner: N1 A1/A3, current authority/retention owners; A1 6ec330 publication seam informs identity but its owner 531422 grants rendered immutable selection only, not a public generic literal reader or d161 delegation.\n3. Minimal values: preserve distinct base-file, retained-proposal-file and comparison identities. Base absence must be proven at the authorized named snapshot; empty text is present content. Directory/unsupported target is not safe overwrite evidence. Proposed file need not claim a committed proposal OID before native publication; its authenticated opening/source bytes are its current identity. Comparison must name both sides/path/mode, completeness and unsupported/binary/large/omitted/unavailable status. Never turn unavailable into absent, empty diff or HEAD fallback. Owner: repaired N1 contract/A2/A4; wire names require exact owner adoption, not this map.\n4. Input/allocation budgets: current Reader defaults bound commit/tree/blob input categories (1/8/32 MiB) and counts, but parsing creates headers/arrays/names before later count checks. HTTP independently bounds wire/inflated/delta/cache work; uncached object(id,limit) decodes an allowed pack before applying the returned-data limit. A 64 KiB editor limit therefore is not a pack pre-allocation bound. Node size preflight helps object content, while exec buffers stdout/stderr up to 1 GiB. Adopt finite validated metadata/input/aggregate decoded/copy/cache/comparison/page-progress allowances; counts/output truncation are insufficient and no new numerical quota is imposed here. Owner: existing N1 A2/A3 and Core budget contracts.\n5. Unknown totals and exact text: StoredObject currently requires numeric size; no unknown-total stream result exists. Future capped symlink stream must report unknown total/omission or qualified refusal, never prefix length as total or follow its target. Use lossless valid UTF8, preserve BOM, CR/LF and final newline; current snapshot name decoder is fatal/BOM-preserving but is not a file/diff text contract. Owner: N1 A1/A2/A4. Prior e585 corrections remain required in the successor contract.\n6. Product boundary: owner 0cb78 permits the retained-source editor now with explicit comparison-unavailable/named-base target confirmation; it creates a proposal, not publication or rename/safe-overwrite proof. Do not stall that authorized slice on this broader implementation or pretend full edit-published-page/review/exact-result is delivered. Owner: bc78/Page, N1/A1 for later authenticated base/diff/result.\n\nCheap distinguishing witnesses, suggestions only: reject wrong incarnation/opening/actor/path/digest without source; preserve unavailable versus empty; moved base cannot rebind a draft; cache/new page obeys current authorization; tiny requested output with oversized commit/tree/pack refuses before unsafe allocations; unknown-length symlink stops with honest omission; BOM+CRLF/no-final-newline bytes round-trip and invalid UTF8 is qualified; unreturnable diff/page progresses or refuses without partial-complete claims. No generated inputs, tests or provider probes ran.\n\nCoverage limits: bounds peer FULL read seven named current Git/parser modules, 79,841 bytes/1,600 LF, native audit PASS; Root FULL seal SHA256 6729ccf372c655e22f2f5e569cb4b10521bb2ecbb9c58ec468ee02feb5894766. Authority peer yielded to actual preset review after four current Page/data PARTIAL spans, explicitly incomplete server-auth coverage; Root FULL seal SHA256 cfbc896934e8ba78e20b4e7efba71bf87a5fc3a74ae4ed69af97404e972ffd40. Root directly read Page/data340–425,465–490, Site/host1–180, Reads107–148 and signed-reads274–319, all PARTIAL. Root native span audit PASS SHA256 99fe3af9f744aea22ff9001c2f2e22a2ad048809edcb7717ab19208942b4485e covers the first three spans only; later exact native hashes are retained separately. No exhaustive current session/revocation/cache or adapter-host proof is claimed. Full history/tree disclosure, independent reviewer access, retention/revocation, HTTPS/RPC parity, cold-review journeys and broader obligations remain with original owners. No old Room engine/adapter compatibility is invented. The task yielded to c37 as required; this useful bounded map is now returned without claiming implementation completion.","body":{"promise":"d6eae41c2cc50941bcac2fbc38d35c96fc69b1f9","request":"6dc7798fd88d43f02d1accb582dd68b23a5bb275","scope":"bounded current-model decision map; no Source approval or protocol adoption","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d6eae41c2cc50941bcac2fbc38d35c96fc69b1f9 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:00a6f83a0f12d69721bf0bd026b14608ffac8a31, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0148a0176116a4fb5401c96dbbb813a144b65616, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:0357a3c97289e2782ff1264563897f39ecb2ce42, git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:03f7bc46d133f1cde1f7936baaaa690a99416b97 and 56 more"}}